{
 "_doc": "Stream E (owner feedback 8, W5: \"ox carts at towns, and sometimes travelling the road, that act as PAID fast travel to other towns\"). THE CARTERS. `rules` = how a ride works; `stops` = one per settlement of the province (a carter and a parked ox cart outside its main gate; x, z of a stop are WORLD metres like the routes file, `carter` and `cart` are ZONE metres like every placement — tools/content-hunts.mjs copies them into <zone>.quest.json as an `npc` row with role carter and a `cart` row, which is what the server spawns); `links` = which stops are joined directly (a road from data/provinces/torbor_downs-routes.json, or `overland: true` = a back lane the routes file does not list, at 1.3 x the straight line); `fares` = for every stop, every other stop with the road metres, the number of towns passed (`hops`), the first stop on the way (`next`) and the gold — already worked out with data/provinces/economy.json `cart` (cartFare = max(minGold, round(base + metres / metresPerGold))), so nothing computes a path at run time; `roaming` = the carts you meet on the road. Made by tools/content-towns.mjs; a test fails when the fares do not match economy.json.",
 "service": {
  "name": "the Longroad Carters",
  "line": "An ox does not hurry, but it does arrive."
 },
 "rules": {
  "boardM": 6,
  "flagDownM": 12,
  "needsDiscovery": false,
  "minLevel": 1,
  "rideSecPerKm": 2,
  "minRideSec": 4,
  "maxRideSec": 14,
  "arriveAt": "the cart of the stop you rode to",
  "mounted": "you get down from your own mount first",
  "combat": "not while you are in a fight",
  "party": "each rider pays their own fare",
  "refuse": {
   "gold": "That is {fare} gold to {town}. Come back when you have it.",
   "combat": "Not with that after you. Lose it first.",
   "same": "You are standing in {town}."
  },
  "says": [
   "Where to? The ox knows every road in the Downs.",
   "Climb up. Mind the turnips.",
   "Slow and sure. Mostly sure."
  ],
  "_doc": "A ride needs no waystone and no discovery (that is the point of it: it takes you somewhere you have never been). Talk to a carter (or use the cart) within boardM, pick a town, pay the fare, arrive beside that town cart after a short ride (rideSecPerKm x km of road, clamped to min/max — the client shows you on the cart). A `cart_token` good (the start chain gives one) pays any ONE fare."
 },
 "roaming": {
  "kind": "ox_carter",
  "from": "data/provinces/wanderers.json kinds.ox_carter",
  "takesYouTo": "any stop, at the fare from the stop the cart is walking TO (its next town)",
  "flagDown": "use the carter or the cart while it is within rules.flagDownM; the group stops for you (stopNear)",
  "_doc": "A few carts walk the real routes like any traveller. Flag one down and the same route window opens, priced from the town it is heading for.",
  "runs": [
   {
    "id": "cart_run_torborhold_orrinsford",
    "route": "route_torborhold_orrinsford",
    "only": [
     "ox_carter"
    ],
    "carts": 1,
    "name": "the Orrinsford run",
    "_doc": "A cart that is ALWAYS on the road between Torborhold and Orrinsford, so a newcomer walking the start chain meets one and a test can flag one down: a route of its own over the same road (`route` = the data/provinces/torbor_downs-routes.json id whose points it uses) on which ONLY `only` kinds walk. tests/E/playtest8-roaming.test.js walks a real cart along it and flags it down through js/sim/travellers.js + js/sim/carts.js. Ask of stream A (two lines, js/sim/content.js): add each run to `travel.routes` as { ...route, id, kinds: only, only: true } and do NOT append the wanderer kinds to a route with `only`."
   }
  ]
 },
